@*
    What this table is, and the seed it came out of. Closed, because it answers questions a
    player asks once and a developer asks often.

    🔥 The second of the three places prose is allowed to live (BUILD-PLAN P13.5). The page used
    to open with three sentences about pace and concealment and follow them with a line about
    the seed. None of it is wrong and none of it belongs on the felt.

    ⚠️ The seed stays reachable rather than being deleted: it is how a match gets reported, and
    `--seed` deals the same one again (P14, §3.9).
*@

<details class="about">
    <summary>
        <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">i</span>
        <span class="what">About this table</span>
    </summary>

    <p>
        A round at a time, at a pace you can follow. Every hand is concealed until somebody lays
        all thirteen down (RULES.md §7.1) — so you are shown your own and nobody else's, and
        anyone here only to watch is shown none at all. Nothing ends a match: the next round is
        dealt on top of the banks (§7.2).
    </p>

    @*
        🔥 What the seats are doing, which no view said until now (RULES.md §3 step 2). P36 held
        the seating and left this a leftover; P37 made it a thing a person can change, so it is
        also a thing they have to be able to find out.
    *@
    <p class="seats">
        @Seating
    </p>

    <p class="seed">
        Seed <strong>@Seed</strong> — every card in this match comes out of it, and
        <code>--seed @Seed</code> deals it again.
    </p>

    <p>
        <a href="rules">How it is played</a>
    </p>
</details>

@code {
    /// <summary>The one seed this whole table is reproducible from.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public int Seed { get; set; }

    /// <summary>How long this table's seating holds (RULES.md §3 step 2).</summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// ⚠️ <b>A policy and not the rule about changing seats.</b> Held is the rule; a table may
    /// also have been opened with a house arrangement, and a person looking at the felt cannot
    /// otherwise tell which (P36, P37).
    /// </remarks>
    [Parameter]
    public SeatingPolicy? Seats { get; set; }

    private string Seating => (Seats ?? SeatingPolicy.Default) switch
    {
        { RoundsBetweenSeatings: 0 } =>
            "The seats were drawn once and stay as they are — until everybody at the table agrees to "
            + "change them, which is what the buttons under your hand are for.",
        var policy =>
            $"The seats are {policy.Description}, and the table can also agree to change them between "
            + "deals."
    };
}
